# The code points that a shown text of air-apps writes as \u{<hex>}: each one of the general categories Cc, Cf, Cn, Co,
# Cs, Zl, Zp and Zs, by Unicode 16.0, as Character.getType of the JDK 25 gives them. The shown text keeps U+0020, which is Zs.
# One range on each line: <first>..<last> or <one>, in upper-case hex, then its category, in the order of the code points.
# air-apps embeds this file (src/shown.rs), and a test of the IDE compares it with the JDK.
